                <pb facs="1025" n="905" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg905"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2589: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Harbin</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-07-17T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 17, 1922—3
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>For Stevens:</p>
                <p>In view of announced purpose of Japan to withdraw troops and the consequent
                    automatic termination of the railway agreement I have deemed it necessary to
                    take up with the Japanese and British Governments in a preliminary confidential
                    manner the question of winding up the Inter-Allied Committee and Technical Board
                    and of confirming the attitude of the Powers toward the Chinese Eastern Railway
                    as outlined at the Washington Conference. Is there any nearer prospect of
                    developments such as you refer to in your June 29, 8 a.m.?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
